cmd-fstutorial-desc = Opens the tutorial for your current job.
cmd-fstutorial-help = Usage: fstutorial [tutorial id]

fs-tutorial-eng-1-title = Your job: hold the line
fs-tutorial-eng-1-text = Zombies come in waves. Your barricades and sentries decide where they hit and how long it takes them. A barricade blocks the edge it faces, and bullets fly over it, so your team shoots from behind it.
    Flames go over barricades too. They don't stop Flamethrowers.
fs-tutorial-eng-2-title = Build with the RCD
fs-tutorial-eng-2-text = Press [bold]Z[/bold] to pick a piece, [bold]click[/bold] to build, [bold]R[/bold] to rotate. Costs come from the materials you carry, then from any silo within 20 tiles.
    The middle of the menu shows what you have against what you need. If a spot is refused, the reason is written under the ghost. Prefer a hotbar? Switch to the belt layout from the menu.
fs-tutorial-eng-3-title = Upgrade with the hammer
fs-tutorial-eng-3-text = Click a barricade with your hammer (or press [bold]E[/bold] on it) to choose an upgrade. You start hammering it in right away; each hit pours in materials from your pack. Click it again to carry on if you stop.
    Grades: [bold]steel[/bold], then [bold]plasteel[/bold], then [bold]depleted uranium[/bold] for the toughest barricades.
    Branches, one per barricade: [bold]Bulwark[/bold] for chokepoints, [bold]Firing Step[/bold] for your gunline, [bold]Floodlit[/bold] for dark lanes. [bold]Barbed wire[/bold] goes on top: it cuts and slows zombies that hit it, but not next to a door. Hits don't count while it's under attack.
fs-tutorial-eng-4-title = Keep it standing
fs-tutorial-eng-4-text = Your [bold]rivet gun[/bold] repairs any barricade it hits, up to the red mark on its health bar, and feeds itself steel from your pack. It works mid-fight.
    For the last stretch, [bold]fit plates and weld them in[/bold]. Engineers see a health bar over every damaged fortification; one that flashes is close to falling.
fs-tutorial-eng-5-title = Sentries
fs-tutorial-eng-5-text = Build sentries with the RCD. They run until their ammo is gone.
    Use the hammer on a sentry to fit modules: longer belts, faster servos, better optics, and hardened or depleted uranium rounds. Modules are paid in the rare materials zombies drop.
fs-tutorial-eng-hmg-title = Heavy machine guns
fs-tutorial-eng-hmg-text = Build an HMG and an ammo crate with the RCD, then drag the crate next to the gun. Anyone can crew it: click the gun to take the seat.
    It covers a 90° arc and overheats if you hold the trigger too long. A line shows which crate feeds which gun.
fs-tutorial-eng-emplacement-title = The emplacement
fs-tutorial-eng-emplacement-text = The Chief Engineer carries a [bold]defensive emplacement[/bold]: a sandbag ring with two sentries that never run dry while its crate has rounds, and a crate that refills magazines.
    Press [bold]Z[/bold] with the kit, turn it with [bold]R[/bold] so the open side faces your team, then click. Anyone inside takes less melee damage. It folds back to the Chief Engineer when the wave ends.
fs-tutorial-eng-broadsword-title = The Broadsword
fs-tutorial-eng-broadsword-text = Once Science researches the [bold]Mech Bay[/bold], build one with the RCD away from the line. Engineering welds the frame, limbs and armour in from your pack; Science fits the control core and targeting module between your stages. Examine the bay to see whose turn it is.
    Build guns at the bay with alt-click. The Broadsword takes three: light and medium guns in any mix, and at most one heavy. Park the Broadsword on the bay to recharge and repair it. In a fight, use [bold]siege mode[/bold] to plant it: it can't move, but it takes far less damage, especially from the front, and your rivet gun can patch it.
fs-tutorial-eng-6-title = Getting paid
fs-tutorial-eng-6-text = You earn credits when your structures soak wave damage and when you repair that damage. Rivet hits on zombies pay too.
    Bring the materials you pick up to the silo so every engineer can build from them. The silo is also restocked at the start of every prep. Your Fortify score is on the leaderboard.
    Ask Science for the Engineering research branch: faster rivets, cooler HMGs, razor wire and the field tools all come from there.

fs-tutorial-welcome-title = Welcome to Final Stand
fs-tutorial-welcome-body = Zombies come in waves. Your job: keep the [bold]Central Command Console[/bold] standing and stay alive. Make it to wave 30 and the round is won.
fs-tutorial-prep-title = Prep phase
fs-tutorial-prep-body = Spend credits at the wall shops like this one for guns, armour and grenades. Ready up when you're set, or the timer starts the wave.
fs-tutorial-first-wave-title = Here they come
fs-tutorial-first-wave-body = Hold together near the console and watch the lanes. Press [bold]{$reload}[/bold] to reload. Running low? The [bold]Ammo Resupply Box[/bold] refills your magazines once per wave. Every kill pays credits.
fs-tutorial-downed-title = You're down
fs-tutorial-downed-body = A teammate can patch you up, or you can pay credits to revive now. Medics earn credits for every heal, so don't be shy about calling for one.
fs-tutorial-perks-title = Wave cleared
fs-tutorial-perks-body = You're earning XP and perk points. Spend them at the [bold]Perk Machine[/bold] before the next wave.
fs-tutorial-dark-wave-title = Dark wave
fs-tutorial-dark-wave-body = The power's out. Survive until the timer runs out instead of killing everything. Stay together and light the way.
fs-tutorial-boss-wave-title = Boss wave
fs-tutorial-boss-wave-body = Every fifth wave brings something big. Focus fire on it and keep moving; killing it pays perk points to everyone.
fs-tutorial-runner-title = Runners
fs-tutorial-runner-body = Runners close the gap fast but go down quickly. Watch your flanks and don't let them reach whoever is reloading or healing.
fs-tutorial-armoured-title = Armoured zombie
fs-tutorial-armoured-body = When it glows, shots bounce back as shrapnel. Hold fire until the glow fades, then unload while it's exposed.
fs-tutorial-bloater-title = Bloater
fs-tutorial-bloater-body = Bloaters burst when they die, poisoning and slowing everyone nearby. Kill them at range and never in the middle of your group.
fs-tutorial-flamethrower-title = Flamethrower zombie
fs-tutorial-flamethrower-body = It winds up, then sprays a cone of fire about five tiles long. Step out of the cone when you see the wind-up, and put fires out fast.
fs-tutorial-tesla-title = Tesla zombie
fs-tutorial-tesla-body = Its lightning jumps from one player to the people standing next to them. Spread out so one zap doesn't hit the whole team.
fs-tutorial-devastator-title = Devastator
fs-tutorial-devastator-body = The more you hurt it, the faster and harder it hits. It shrugs off stuns and heals on every hit, so focus it down in one push.
fs-tutorial-revenant-title = Revenant
fs-tutorial-revenant-body = Revenants hunt players who stray from the group, phase through cover and drag their prey away. Stay together and cover anyone it marks.
fs-tutorial-controls-title = Controls
fs-tutorial-controls-body =
    Press [bold]{$reload}[/bold] to reload from the ammo you carry.
    Press [bold]{$suit}[/bold] to stow or draw your suit storage item.
    Press [bold]{$grenade}[/bold] to throw a live grenade at your cursor.
    Press [bold]{$ping}[/bold] to ping a spot for your team.
fs-tutorial-perk-shop-title = The Perk Machine
fs-tutorial-perk-shop-body = Perk points from levelling up buy permanent upgrades here. Not sure what to pick? A starter build buys and slots a full set in one click.
fs-tutorial-grenades-title = Grenades
fs-tutorial-grenades-body = You've got grenades. Press [bold]{$grenade}[/bold] to throw one live at your cursor, no need to take it out first. Use the grenade action to switch type.
fs-tutorial-ccc-attacked-title = The console is under attack
fs-tutorial-ccc-attacked-body = Zombies are hitting the [bold]Central Command Console[/bold]. If it's destroyed, the round is lost. Kill whatever is on it first. It heals a little after each wave.
fs-tutorial-ready-up-title = Ready up
fs-tutorial-ready-up-body = Done shopping? Press [bold]YES[/bold] under [bold]Ready up[/bold] on the right. When everyone is ready, the next wave starts early and you skip the wait.
fs-tutorial-unbound = unbound
fs-tutorial-dismiss = Got it
fs-tutorial-footer = Type "tutorial off" in the console to hide these tips.

cmd-tutorial-desc = Turns the new-player tips on or off, or replays them.
cmd-tutorial-help = Usage: tutorial [on|off|replay]
cmd-tutorial-hint = on, off or replay
cmd-tutorial-no-player = Only players get tutorial tips.
cmd-tutorial-on = Tutorial tips are on.
cmd-tutorial-off = Tutorial tips are off.
cmd-tutorial-replay = Tutorial tips will show again from the start.
cmd-tutorial-status-on = Tutorial tips are on. Use "tutorial off" to hide them.
cmd-tutorial-status-off = Tutorial tips are off. Use "tutorial on" to see them.
